<title>CHILE: Chile's Copec H1 net rises slightly.</title>
<headline>Chile's Copec H1 net rises slightly.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forestry and gasoline distribution conglomerate Compania de Petroleos de Chile SA, Copec, reported the following results in the first half of the year.</p>
<p>			   H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p> Net earnings	     60.82	     58.40</p>
<p> Operating income	 11.62	     12.93</p>
<p> Non-operating income   51.04	     46.98</p>
<p> Total sales	     368.63	    324.79</p>
<p>NOTE: 1. New Zealand forestry firm Carter Holt Harvey owns 30 percent of Copec.</p>
<p>2.  All figures are in billions of pesos. (( --Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
